# -- your real, personal config -- never tracked, never overwritten --------
# Generic placeholders ship as the *.example versions (tracked); your real,
# filled-in versions keep their normal filenames on disk and are simply
# invisible to git. Nothing in this project (my-bt, the RPM, build/install
# scripts) ever deletes or overwrites these -- see README.md and the
# maintainer's local notes for the full reasoning.
/settings.toml
/site/index.html
/site/impressum.html
/site/privacy.html
/site/privacy.html.tmpl
/site/terms.html
/site/nginx-locations.conf
/site/index_embedded.html

# ...or keep that whole set together in ONE directory named `*.local`
# instead (e.g. my-booking.local/settings.toml,
# my-booking.local/site/index.html), which the two rules at the bottom of
# this file already cover. Every lookup prefers it -- see
# app/local_overlay.py. The per-path rules above stay regardless, so the
# ordinary layout keeps working and stays unpublishable either way.

# -- runtime/local state -----------------------------------------------------
/data/
/secrets/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# -- local build output -------------------------------------------------------
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/

# -- editor/OS cruft -----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Local-only files: never published, carried between machines by
# the container repo (see its .git.force-add-patterns).
*.local
*.local.*
